      "first": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "Every story when we were children revealed a lesson,"
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 794,
        "text": "When I think of myself, I remember my canning jar of poisoned sausage. I can’t say I forgive my father, but I safeguard above all else, the ability that canning jar gives me, to imagine the unthinkable urge that possessed him, taking him into the very darkness."
